6.1E The Provenance Logic: Complete Fragment Definition

We now provide a complete formal definition of Provenance Logic (PL) as a dedicated formal system for reasoning about the causal chain of AI administrative decisions.

Definition 6.1E (Provenance Logic PL). PL is a three-sorted logic over the sorts: Agent (AI agents, human officials, and the FVAL system itself), Fact (ground facts about the world at a specific time), and Decision (administrative decision events).

The primitive predicates of PL are:

Asserts(a, f, t, src) — agent a asserts fact f at time t, where src is the GKG node that is the authoritative source of f.

Derives(a, δ, {f₁,...,fₙ}, {r₁,...,rₘ}, t) — agent a derives draft decision δ at time t from facts {f₁,...,fₙ} by applying rules {r₁,...,rₘ}.

Certifies(FVAL, δ, t_cert) — the FVAL system issues an LCC for decision δ at time t_cert.

Authorizes(h, δ, t_auth) — human official h authorizes decision δ at time t_auth.

Supersedes(δ₂, δ₁, t) — decision δ₂ supersedes decision δ₁ (on appeal or correction) at time t.

InForceAt(r, t) — rule r is in legal force at time t.

SatisfiedBy(r.condition, ctx, t) — the condition of rule r is satisfied by context ctx at time t.

ActiveException(r, ctx, t) — an exception clause of rule r is activated by ctx at time t.

PermissibleOutcome(δ.outcome, r, ctx) — the outcome of δ is among the deontic consequences authorized by rule r given context ctx.

PL formulas are built from these predicates using standard first-order connectives and quantification over the three sorts.

A complete provenance record for a decision δ is a PL theory T(δ) — a set of closed PL sentences — satisfying:

P1 (Fact Grounding): For every fact fᵢ used in deriving δ, T(δ) contains Asserts(aᵢ, fᵢ, tᵢ, srcᵢ) for some agent aᵢ, time tᵢ, and GKG source srcᵢ.

P2 (Rule Invocation): T(δ) contains Derives(α, δ, {f₁,...,fₙ}, {r₁,...,rₘ}, t_derive) for the specific agent α and derivation time t_derive.

P3 (Rule Validity): For each rⱼ in the derivation, T(δ) contains InForceAt(rⱼ, t_derive).

P4 (Condition Satisfaction): For each rⱼ, T(δ) contains SatisfiedBy(rⱼ.condition, ctx, t_derive).

P5 (Exception Absence): For each rⱼ, T(δ) contains ¬ActiveException(rⱼ, ctx, t_derive).

P6 (Outcome Permissibility): T(δ) contains PermissibleOutcome(δ.outcome, rⱼ, ctx) for at least one rⱼ in the derivation.

P7 (Certification): T(δ) contains Certifies(FVAL, δ, t_cert) for some t_cert ≥ t_derive.

P8 (Authorization): T(δ) contains Authorizes(h, δ, t_auth) for some human official h and t_auth ≥ t_cert (for Level B and Level C decisions; for Level A decisions, Authorizes is replaced by a system audit event).

Theorem 6.1 (PL Completeness for Legal Accountability). A decision δ is legally accountable — that is, its full causal chain from factual inputs through rule application to authorized outcome can be reconstructed and verified by an independent tribunal — if and only if T(δ) is a complete provenance theory satisfying P1 through P8.

Proof sketch. Necessity: If any of P1–P8 fails, a gap in the accountability chain exists. If P1 fails, the factual basis of δ cannot be independently verified. If P2 fails, the derivation logic is opaque. If P3 fails, the rule may not have been legally in force. If P4 fails, the legal condition was not actually met. If P5 fails, an applicable exception was ignored. If P6 fails, the outcome exceeds legal authorization. If P7 fails, the decision was not formally verified. If P8 fails, no authorized human takes responsibility for the decision. Any of these gaps creates a defect in legal accountability.

Sufficiency: Given T(δ) satisfying P1–P8, an independent tribunal can reconstruct: what facts were used (P1), how they led to the decision (P2), whether the invoked rules were legally valid (P3), whether their conditions were actually met (P4), whether exceptions were correctly handled (P5), whether the outcome is within the law (P6), whether formal verification occurred (P7), and who bears institutional responsibility (P8). This constitutes complete legal accountability. □

6.2E Pseudocode for the Three Verification Checks

We now provide complete pseudocode for each verification check. These specifications are intended to be directly implementable.

ALGORITHM: V1_LegalConformance

Input: δ_draft (draft decision), ctx (context record), R (normative ruleset), t (decision time)
Output: (passed: boolean, diagnosis: V1Diagnosis)

BEGIN
  diagnosis ← new V1Diagnosis()
  legal_basis ← δ_draft.legal_basis   // set of rule IDs claimed by the agent
  
  FOR EACH rule_id IN legal_basis DO
    r ← R.lookup(rule_id)
    
    // Check P3: Rule in force
    IF NOT InForceAt(r, t) THEN
      diagnosis.add_failure(RULE_NOT_IN_FORCE, rule_id, t)
      RETURN (false, diagnosis)
    END IF
    
    // Check P4: Condition satisfied
    eval_result ← ARDL_Evaluate(r.condition, ctx, t)
    IF NOT eval_result.satisfied THEN
      diagnosis.add_failure(CONDITION_NOT_MET, rule_id, eval_result.counterexample)
      RETURN (false, diagnosis)
    END IF
    
    // Check P5: No active exception
    FOR EACH exc IN r.exceptions DO
      exc_result ← ARDL_Evaluate(exc, ctx, t)
      IF exc_result.satisfied THEN
        diagnosis.add_failure(EXCEPTION_ACTIVE, rule_id, exc, exc_result.witness)
        RETURN (false, diagnosis)
      END IF
    END FOR
    
    // Check P6: Outcome permissible
    permissible_outcomes ← DeonticExpand(r.obligation, ctx)
    IF δ_draft.outcome NOT IN permissible_outcomes THEN
      diagnosis.add_failure(OUTCOME_NOT_PERMISSIBLE, rule_id,
                            δ_draft.outcome, permissible_outcomes)
      RETURN (false, diagnosis)
    END IF
    

  END FOR
  
  diagnosis.all_passed = true
  RETURN (true, diagnosis)
END

FUNCTION ARDL_Evaluate(formula, ctx, t):
  // Evaluate ARDL formula against context record at time t
  // Returns {satisfied: boolean, counterexample or witness}
  // Uses the GKG query interface for fact lookup
  // Temporal evaluation uses the event trace in ctx
  RETURN standard LTL model-checking over finite trace ctx.event_trace

FUNCTION DeonticExpand(obligation_formula, ctx):
  // Returns the set of concrete outcomes that satisfy the deontic obligation
  // given the context. For simple obligation types (approve/reject/set-value),
  // this returns a finite enumerable set.
  ...

---

ALGORITHM: V2_ProceduralCorrectness

Input: δ_draft, workflow_path (sequence of node IDs traversed), W (workflow graph), ctx
Output: (passed: boolean, diagnosis: V2Diagnosis)

BEGIN
  diagnosis ← new V2Diagnosis()
  
  // Verify workflow_path is a valid path in W
  FOR i FROM 0 TO length(workflow_path) - 2 DO
    current_node ← workflow_path[i]
    next_node ← workflow_path[i+1]
    
    // Check edge exists
    IF NOT W.has_edge(current_node, next_node) THEN
      diagnosis.add_failure(INVALID_TRANSITION, current_node, next_node)
      RETURN (false, diagnosis)
    END IF
    
    // Check guard satisfied
    guard ← W.get_guard(current_node, next_node)
    IF guard != NULL AND NOT EvaluateGuard(guard, ctx) THEN
      diagnosis.add_failure(GUARD_NOT_SATISFIED, current_node, next_node, guard)
      RETURN (false, diagnosis)
    END IF
    
  END FOR
  
  // Verify final node is a Decision node
  final_node ← workflow_path[last]
  IF W.get_type(final_node) != DECISION THEN
    diagnosis.add_failure(WRONG_TERMINAL_TYPE, final_node, W.get_type(final_node))
    RETURN (false, diagnosis)
  END IF

  
  // Verify no required intermediate nodes were skipped
  required_nodes ← W.get_mandatory_nodes(workflow_path[0], final_node)
  FOR EACH req IN required_nodes DO
    IF req NOT IN workflow_path THEN
      diagnosis.add_failure(REQUIRED_NODE_SKIPPED, req)
      RETURN (false, diagnosis)
    END IF
  END FOR
  
  diagnosis.all_passed = true
  RETURN (true, diagnosis)
END

---

ALGORITHM: V3_NormativeCompleteness

Input: δ_draft, ctx, R, t, domain_tag (administrative domain)
Output: (passed: boolean, omitted_rules: List[RuleID], diagnosis: V3Diagnosis)

BEGIN
  diagnosis ← new V3Diagnosis()
  omitted_rules ← []
  
  // Retrieve candidate rules from relevance index
  candidate_rules ← RelevanceIndex.lookup(domain_tag, ctx.entity_types)
  
  FOR EACH r IN candidate_rules DO
  
    // Skip rules already in legal_basis
    IF r.id IN δ_draft.legal_basis THEN
      CONTINUE
    END IF
    
    // Check if rule condition is satisfied by ctx
    eval_result ← ARDL_Evaluate(r.condition, ctx, t)
    IF eval_result.satisfied THEN
    
      // Rule is relevant but not cited — potential omission
      // Check whether citing it would change the outcome
      impact ← DeonticImpact(r, δ_draft.outcome, ctx)
      
      IF impact == CHANGES_OUTCOME THEN
        // Serious omission: rule changes the decision
        omitted_rules.add(r.id)
        diagnosis.add_failure(OUTCOME_ALTERING_OMISSION, r.id, impact)
        
      ELSE IF impact == REQUIRES_CITATION THEN
        // Non-outcome-altering but legally required citation
        omitted_rules.add(r.id)
        diagnosis.add_failure(REQUIRED_CITATION_MISSING, r.id)
        
      ELSE
        // Rule is satisfied but legitimately not dispositive — log but do not fail
        diagnosis.add_note(NON_DISPOSITIVE_RULE_SATISFIED, r.id)
      END IF
      
    END IF
    

  END FOR
  
  IF length(omitted_rules) > 0 THEN
    // Log as normative gap if no applicable rule exists in R for this pattern
    IF ALL omitted_rules ARE non_dispositive THEN
      NormativeGapLog.record(ctx.pattern_hash, omitted_rules, t)
      RETURN (true, omitted_rules, diagnosis)  // soft pass with noted gaps
    ELSE
      RETURN (false, omitted_rules, diagnosis)  // hard fail
    END IF
  END IF
  
  RETURN (true, [], diagnosis)
END

FUNCTION DeonticImpact(r, current_outcome, ctx):
  // Determines what impact r has on the current outcome
  // Returns: CHANGES_OUTCOME | REQUIRES_CITATION | NON_DISPOSITIVE
  projected ← DeonticExpand(r.obligation, ctx)
  IF current_outcome NOT IN projected THEN
    RETURN CHANGES_OUTCOME
  ELSE IF r.citation_required_by_law THEN
    RETURN REQUIRES_CITATION
  ELSE
    RETURN NON_DISPOSITIVE

---

ALGORITHM: LCC_Generation

Input: δ_draft, ctx, v1_result, v2_result, v3_result, workflow_path, t_verify
Output: LCC (Legal Conformance Certificate)

BEGIN
  IF NOT (v1_result.passed AND v2_result.passed AND v3_result.passed) THEN
    RETURN RefusalWithDiagnosis(δ_draft, v1_result, v2_result, v3_result)
  END IF
  
  // Build provenance record (the PL theory T(δ))
  prov ← new ProvenanceRecord()
  
  // P1: Fact grounding
  FOR EACH (fact, source_node) IN ctx.fact_sources DO
    prov.add( Asserts(ctx.agent_id, fact, source_node.certified_at, source_node.gkg_id) )
  END FOR
  
  // P2: Derivation record
  prov.add( Derives(ctx.agent_id, δ_draft, ctx.facts, δ_draft.legal_basis, ctx.derivation_time) )
  
  // P3–P6: Rule verification records (from V1 results)
  FOR EACH rule_check IN v1_result.rule_checks DO
    prov.add( InForceAt(rule_check.rule_id, t_verify) )
    prov.add( SatisfiedBy(rule_check.rule_id + ".condition", ctx, t_verify) )
    prov.add( Neg(ActiveException(rule_check.rule_id, ctx, t_verify)) )
    prov.add( PermissibleOutcome(δ_draft.outcome, rule_check.rule_id, ctx) )
  END FOR

  
  // P7: Certification event
  prov.add( Certifies(FVAL_SYSTEM_ID, δ_draft.case_id, t_verify) )
  
  // Generate natural language legal summary
  lang_code ← ctx.jurisdiction.primary_language
  legal_summary ← NLG_Engine.generate(prov, lang_code, jurisdiction_procedure_law)
  
  // Compute decision hash
  d_hash ← SHA256(serialize(δ_draft))
  
  // Assemble LCC
  lcc ← new LCC(
    case_id = δ_draft.case_id,
    decision_hash = d_hash,
    jurisdiction = ctx.jurisdiction,
    verification_timestamp = t_verify,
    agent_id = ctx.agent_id,
    verification_engine_version = FVAL.version,
    v1_legal_conformance = v1_result,
    v2_procedural_correctness = v2_result,
    v3_normative_completeness = v3_result,
    provenance_record = prov,
    legal_summary = legal_summary,
    technical_signature = FVAL.sign(d_hash + serialize(prov) + t_verify)
  )

  
  // Add LCC to documentary corpus and Audit Ledger
  DMI.store(lcc, type=VERIFICATION_CERTIFICATE, provenance=[δ_draft.case_id])
  IAL.append(lcc)
  
  RETURN lcc
END

